//OUT="0 2 4 6 8 "

// The one place `cnt` could go wrong. A `for` is lowered into
//
//     $it = x.iter()
//     while $it.has_next()
//         i = $it.next()
//         <body>
//
// so the advance is the first statement of the loop body, not part of the
// loop's own machinery. `cnt` has to land before it — jumping to the
// condition, as it does in a `while` — or the loop would spin on one element
// forever. Skipping to the odd values and back proves it moves on.

fn main
    for i 0..10
        if i % 2 == 1
            cnt
        out "{i} "
